#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Chapultepec: the storming of the castle and the gates of Mexico City,
12-13 September 1847.  A sample game for the Grognard engine.

Winfield Scott's army has fought its way from Veracruz to the edge of
Mexico City.  Between it and the western gates stands the hill of
Chapultepec and the castle on top, home of the Military College.  A day
of bombardment, then the storm: up through the cypress grove and over
the walls with scaling ladders, then along the causeways across the wet
meadows to the Belén and San Cosme gates.  Play either side against the
computer, or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./chapultepec (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.chapultepec.json.  ./chapultepec --selftest checks the map
and plays a game between two computer players.
"""

